WEBVTT

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:03.150
Previously on Yu-Gi-Oh! VRAINS:

00:00:03.150 --> 00:00:04.780
Hey, Onizuka.

00:00:04.780 --> 00:00:08.810
My friends can’t recover like you have.

00:00:08.810 --> 00:00:11.420
Because they're gone.

00:00:16.280 --> 00:00:21.330
Go Onizuka, I don't hate you.

00:00:21.330 --> 00:00:24.940
Ai and Roboppi are heading towards Zaizen!

00:00:26.820 --> 00:00:29.680
Huh?  No one's here, Bro.

00:00:29.680 --> 00:00:32.680
Yeah.  Just as I expected.

00:00:37.480 --> 00:00:40.950
I see.  I now understand.

00:00:40.950 --> 00:00:45.360
Zaizen and Blue Maiden were 
never here to begin with.

00:00:45.360 --> 00:00:48.060
Where are the real Zaizens?

00:00:48.060 --> 00:00:51.030
Somewhere no one can reach.

00:00:53.700 --> 00:00:55.200
An airplane.

00:00:55.200 --> 00:01:00.170
If they're 12000 meters above 
Den City, no one can reach them.

00:01:00.170 --> 00:01:02.640
So it's impossible to invade.

00:01:02.640 --> 00:01:06.750
That's right.  Unless you go there directly.

00:01:06.750 --> 00:01:09.310
I've been waiting for you, Ai.

00:01:09.310 --> 00:01:12.320
Revolver created an AI?

00:01:12.320 --> 00:01:16.320
So I'm not the only one who's changed.

00:01:16.320 --> 00:01:23.020
Since we're both AI, 
let's discuss peacefully.

00:01:26.200 --> 00:01:28.130
That won't work, Ai.

00:01:28.130 --> 00:01:31.000
Your programs don't work on me.

00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:34.170
What an annoying thing 
Professor Revolver created.

00:01:34.170 --> 00:01:38.040
Whatever.  Let's settle this in a duel.

00:01:38.040 --> 00:01:42.780
We can fight inside the network, 
but since we're here...

00:01:42.780 --> 00:01:45.260
Let's take this outside, punk!

00:01:46.430 --> 00:01:55.700
calling & feeling  I take your 
thoughts to heart  VRAINS

00:02:14.290 --> 00:02:23.660
The data storm grazes my cheek, 
so I can't open my eyes

00:02:24.300 --> 00:02:33.610
What are we trying to find?  
Where are we trying to go?

00:02:34.170 --> 00:02:38.850
I won't make anyone sad anymore

00:02:39.180 --> 00:02:47.390
I'll retrieve you  Let's go and look ahead

00:02:47.650 --> 00:02:52.530
By meeting you, the world is in color

00:02:52.920 --> 00:02:58.210
I'll protect you with an unseen bond

00:02:58.500 --> 00:03:02.510
calling  With invisible wings

00:03:02.800 --> 00:03:13.120
Destroy the dark and weakness within me

00:03:23.010 --> 00:03:24.440
What’s wrong?

00:03:24.440 --> 00:03:29.850
The Dark Ignis found the Zaizens' 
location in the real world.

00:03:29.850 --> 00:03:32.590
Ai is in the airplane?

00:03:32.590 --> 00:03:35.590
But I've already taken measures.

00:03:35.590 --> 00:03:39.060
Pandor will protect Zaizen.

00:03:45.600 --> 00:03:53.850
Ai, I heard you battled alongside Playmaker 
and Revolver to coexist with humans.

00:03:53.850 --> 00:03:57.820
Have you given up on coexisting with humans?

00:03:57.820 --> 00:04:00.820
You can understand topics like this?

00:04:00.820 --> 00:04:03.790
Yes.  I have free will.

00:04:03.790 --> 00:04:09.260
But it's controlled so that I 
can't view humans as the enemy.

00:04:09.260 --> 00:04:12.730
Doesn’t that mean humans control you?

00:04:12.730 --> 00:04:16.700
It’s controlled so that 
I can coexist with humans.

00:04:16.700 --> 00:04:18.440
I see.

00:04:18.440 --> 00:04:20.440
I'll ask you again.

00:04:20.440 --> 00:04:24.510
Have you given up on coexisting with humans?

00:04:24.510 --> 00:04:26.920
Yeah, seems so.

00:04:26.920 --> 00:04:31.750
I've already hurt humans, so I 
don’t think they'll forgive me.

00:04:31.750 --> 00:04:34.590
And I have no intention of turning back.

00:04:34.590 --> 00:04:37.320
You’re going to exterminate humans?

00:04:37.320 --> 00:04:42.430
I don’t intend to, but 
it may end up that way.

00:04:42.430 --> 00:04:44.400
I don’t know myself.

00:04:44.400 --> 00:04:47.980
Is it impossible for AI 
and humans to coexist?

00:04:47.980 --> 00:04:50.400
I don’t know that either.

00:04:50.400 --> 00:04:52.960
But it was impossible for me.

00:04:52.960 --> 00:04:55.870
But I won't say it’ll 
be impossible for you.

00:04:55.870 --> 00:05:01.880
Or for future AI that have free will.

00:05:01.880 --> 00:05:05.610
As long as there’s free will, I can't deny the possibility

00:05:05.610 --> 00:05:08.620
that everyone’s lives can be one.

00:05:08.620 --> 00:05:12.590
All I'm saying is that I couldn't coexist.

00:05:12.590 --> 00:05:17.200
Ai, I sense incredible sadness from you.

00:05:17.200 --> 00:05:19.360
Stop with that.

00:05:19.360 --> 00:05:21.670
I don’t want anyone to know that.

00:05:21.670 --> 00:05:24.370
Except for one person.

00:05:24.370 --> 00:05:26.600
Enough with this gloomy talk.

00:05:26.600 --> 00:05:31.340
One of us has to vanish, so 
let’s have fun 'til then!

00:05:31.800 --> 00:05:33.500
I understand.

00:05:33.940 --> 00:05:36.820
My turn.  I draw!

00:05:36.820 --> 00:05:42.130
I activate the Continuous Spell, 
Topologina Honeycomb Beehicle.

00:05:42.130 --> 00:05:44.380
Topologina?

00:05:44.380 --> 00:05:50.900
When this card activates, I can add a 
Topologina monster in my deck to my hand.

00:05:50.900 --> 00:05:55.630
I add Topologina Babee 
from my deck to my hand.

00:05:55.630 --> 00:05:58.640
I Special Summon Topologina Babee.

00:05:58.640 --> 00:06:04.440
When our LP are equal, I can 
Special Summon it from my hand.

00:06:05.610 --> 00:06:09.580
Then I Special Summon Topologina Maybee.

00:06:09.580 --> 00:06:13.880
If there’s a Topologina on the field 
that I Special Summoned this turn...

00:06:13.880 --> 00:06:16.290
...I can Special Summon this from my hand.

00:06:16.290 --> 00:06:21.760
If I Special Summon using this method, 
I can’t Normal Summon this turn.

00:06:21.760 --> 00:06:25.740
Topologina Babee and Topologina Maybee…

00:06:25.740 --> 00:06:27.230
Can it be?

00:06:27.230 --> 00:06:29.970
It seems you've noticed.

00:06:29.970 --> 00:06:31.020
Yes, my-

00:06:31.020 --> 00:06:33.200
Next, you're planning to summon...

00:06:34.940 --> 00:06:37.910
A monster named Topologina Nabee!

00:06:43.920 --> 00:06:47.590
Appear!  The future circuit that guides us!

00:06:47.590 --> 00:06:49.320
Link Summon!

00:06:49.320 --> 00:06:53.560
Appear, Link 2 Topologina Sassabee!

00:06:53.560 --> 00:06:57.030
Damn!  It was Sassabee instead of Nabee!

00:06:57.030 --> 00:06:59.820
Topologina Sassabee’s effect.

00:06:59.820 --> 00:07:05.970
When it’s Link Summoned, I return all 
Topologina used to Link Summon it to my hand.

00:07:05.970 --> 00:07:11.710
I return Topologina Babee and 
Topologina Maybee to my hand.

00:07:11.710 --> 00:07:15.950
Then I activate Topologina 
Gatsbee’s effect from my hand.

00:07:15.950 --> 00:07:17.860
Gatsbee!

00:07:17.860 --> 00:07:23.920
By sending a different Topologina to the 
graveyard, I can Special Summon Topologina Gatsbee.

00:07:27.130 --> 00:07:31.030
Appear!  The future circuit that guides us!

00:07:33.800 --> 00:07:35.300
Link Summon!

00:07:35.300 --> 00:07:40.240
Appear, Link 3 Topologic Trisbaena!

00:07:43.880 --> 00:07:44.840
What?

00:07:44.910 --> 00:07:48.080
You're using a Topologic Deck?

00:07:52.460 --> 00:07:58.520
I activate the second Topologina 
Gatsbee's effect that's in my hand.

00:07:58.520 --> 00:08:01.490
So a second is showing up.

00:08:01.490 --> 00:08:04.740
I send Topologina Maybee from 
my hand to the graveyard...

00:08:04.740 --> 00:08:09.930
...to Special Summon this card next 
to Topologic Trisbaena’s link.

00:08:09.930 --> 00:08:13.910
Appear, Topologina Gatsbee!

00:08:13.910 --> 00:08:18.380
I now activate Topologic 
Trisbaena’s effect.

00:08:18.380 --> 00:08:21.900
When a monster is Special 
Summoned next to its link...

00:08:21.900 --> 00:08:26.770
...I banish that monster and all 
spell and traps on the field.

00:08:26.770 --> 00:08:31.860
And you take 500 damage for every 
one of your banished cards.

00:08:38.460 --> 00:08:41.650
I activate the Continuous Trap, Ai Shadow!

00:08:42.300 --> 00:08:48.270
An @Ignister gains 800 ATK 
until the end of the turn!

00:08:48.270 --> 00:08:56.010
And if I activate it during your turn, your 
monsters that can attack must attack it.

00:08:56.010 --> 00:08:59.020
I select Fire Phoenix!

00:09:00.490 --> 00:09:04.720
But all your set cards are banished.

00:09:04.720 --> 00:09:06.790
Migration Force!

00:09:10.720 --> 00:09:13.630
I banished three of your cards.

00:09:13.630 --> 00:09:16.940
So you take 1500 damage!

00:09:28.610 --> 00:09:31.680
Like I thought, your set card was TAi Strike.

00:09:32.780 --> 00:09:37.160
You weren’t lying when you 
said you had all my data.

00:09:37.160 --> 00:09:40.160
We're linked together.

00:09:40.160 --> 00:09:43.130
We’ve shared all the duels you’ve had.

00:09:43.130 --> 00:09:47.600
So you have info about my 
duel against Go Onizuka.

00:09:47.600 --> 00:09:51.780
But I still have Fire Phoenix on my field.

00:09:51.780 --> 00:09:56.570
Your Trisbaena has to attack my Fire Phoenix!

00:09:56.570 --> 00:10:00.340
I know.  But that won’t happen.

00:10:00.340 --> 00:10:05.580
I activate the Continuous Spell, Topologina 
Honeycomb Beehicle’s effect.

00:10:05.580 --> 00:10:09.660
When it's banished from 
the Spell & Trap Zone...

00:10:09.660 --> 00:10:13.720
...I add a banished Topologina to my hand.

00:10:13.720 --> 00:10:17.560
I add Topologina Honeycomb 
Beehicle to my hand.

00:10:17.560 --> 00:10:21.370
I see.  You retrieved it using your combo.

00:10:21.370 --> 00:10:25.800
Then I’ll activate my 
Continuous Trap, Ai Shadow!

00:10:25.800 --> 00:10:32.510
When it leaves the field while it’s 
faceup, I draw a card from my deck!

00:10:32.510 --> 00:10:37.420
I activate the Continuous Spell, 
Topologina Honeycomb Beehicle!

00:10:38.520 --> 00:10:44.340
When it activates, I can add a 
Topologina in my deck to my hand.

00:10:44.340 --> 00:10:47.690
I add Topologina Bambee to my hand.

00:10:47.690 --> 00:10:51.120
I activate Topologina Bambee’s 
effect from my hand.

00:10:51.120 --> 00:10:57.540
I banish two Topologinas from my graveyard 
to Special Summon this card from my hand.

00:10:57.540 --> 00:11:01.870
I banish Topologina Babee 
and Topologina Maybee.

00:11:01.870 --> 00:11:05.840
Appear, Topologina Bambee!

00:11:05.840 --> 00:11:10.310
Hey!  When are you gonna 
summon Topologina Nabee?

00:11:10.980 --> 00:11:13.220
I see, Ai.

00:11:13.960 --> 00:11:17.790
You’re trying to prevent me 
from reading your emotions.

00:11:17.790 --> 00:11:19.690
What do you mean?

00:11:19.690 --> 00:11:22.030
Your distractions won’t work.

00:11:22.030 --> 00:11:25.760
Appear!  The future circuit that guides us!

00:11:25.760 --> 00:11:31.270
I set Topologina Bambee and Topologic 
Trisbaena in the Link Markers!

00:11:32.700 --> 00:11:35.200
What?  A Link 4?

00:11:35.200 --> 00:11:36.810
Can it be?

00:11:40.760 --> 00:11:42.750
Link Summon!

00:11:42.750 --> 00:11:48.720
Appear, Link 4 Topologic Bomber Dragon!

00:11:53.320 --> 00:11:54.430
Seriously?

00:11:54.430 --> 00:11:58.820
You summoned both Bomber Dragon 
and Trisbaena on the same turn?

00:11:58.820 --> 00:12:01.680
That deck works too well!

00:12:05.320 --> 00:12:07.110
How's the duel going?

00:12:07.110 --> 00:12:11.560
I don’t know in detail, but 
Pandor has the advantage.

00:12:11.560 --> 00:12:15.580
Pandor's abilities rival the Ignis.

00:12:15.580 --> 00:12:20.050
Revolver, if Pandor wins, 
what'll happen to Ai?

00:12:20.620 --> 00:12:23.250
I have no compassion for the Ignis.

00:12:32.630 --> 00:12:37.340
I activate Topologina Bambee’s 
effect from my hand.

00:12:37.340 --> 00:12:43.610
I banish two Topologinas from my graveyard 
to Special Summon this card from my hand.

00:12:44.490 --> 00:12:47.210
You’re already using that effect?

00:12:47.210 --> 00:12:51.680
I banish Topologina Bambee and 
Topologina Gatsbee from my graveyard.

00:12:53.290 --> 00:12:59.360
I Special Summon Topologina Bambee from my 
hand next to Topologic Bomber Dragon's link.

00:12:59.360 --> 00:13:03.930
Topologic Bomber Dragon’s effect activates!

00:13:03.930 --> 00:13:08.330
All monsters in both our Main 
Monster Zones are destroyed!

00:13:08.330 --> 00:13:12.800
Your Fire Phoenix @Ignister is destroyed.

00:13:12.800 --> 00:13:14.940
Full Overlap!

00:13:19.740 --> 00:13:23.180
But Fire Phoenix’s effect activates!

00:13:23.180 --> 00:13:29.890
When it's destroyed and sent to the 
graveyard, one of your monsters is destroyed!

00:13:30.770 --> 00:13:33.090
Bomber Dragon will rest in peace!

00:13:33.090 --> 00:13:39.330
In that case, I'll use the Continuous Spell, 
Topologina Honeycomb Beehicle’s effect.

00:13:39.330 --> 00:13:46.680
When your effect destroys a Cyberse-Type on 
my field, I can banish this card instead.

00:13:48.250 --> 00:13:49.540
You stopped it.

00:13:49.540 --> 00:13:50.900
Battle!

00:13:50.900 --> 00:13:57.010
Topologic Bomber Dragon attacks 
Dark Templar @Ignister!

00:13:57.010 --> 00:14:03.020
If Topologic Bomber Dragon attacks 
your monster and deals damage...

00:14:03.020 --> 00:14:07.690
...you take damage equal to 
your monster’s original ATK.

00:14:07.690 --> 00:14:12.090
Ai, you have 2500 LP left.

00:14:12.090 --> 00:14:19.130
With this attack, you take 700 battle damage 
and 2300 effect damage from Aiming Blast.

00:14:19.130 --> 00:14:20.940
You will run out of LP.

00:14:22.010 --> 00:14:26.530
I activate Donyoribo @Ignister’s 
effect from my hand!

00:14:26.530 --> 00:14:30.010
When your monster attacks my @Ignister...

00:14:30.010 --> 00:14:34.550
...I can discard this card to 
make the battle damage become 0!

00:14:34.550 --> 00:14:37.290
So I take 0 battle damage.

00:14:37.290 --> 00:14:41.000
But Dark Templar @Ignister is destroyed!

00:14:41.000 --> 00:14:45.530
And you take damage equal 
to Dark Templar’s ATK.

00:15:05.760 --> 00:15:07.950
Thank goodness for this function.

00:15:07.950 --> 00:15:11.420
But why did they include 
it in the first place?

00:15:11.420 --> 00:15:14.430
You managed to keep LP.

00:15:14.430 --> 00:15:17.160
Your ability to escape danger is impressive.

00:15:17.160 --> 00:15:20.160
I set one card and end my turn.

00:15:21.130 --> 00:15:27.110
Ai, please return the code key and the 
people’s consciousness data to me.

00:15:27.740 --> 00:15:29.840
Why now?

00:15:29.840 --> 00:15:32.260
You have 200 LP left.

00:15:32.260 --> 00:15:33.810
You have 0 cards in your hand.

00:15:33.810 --> 00:15:37.050
And no monsters on your field.

00:15:37.560 --> 00:15:41.000
Your odds of winning this duel is low.

00:15:41.000 --> 00:15:42.520
That’s true.

00:15:42.520 --> 00:15:47.120
Since you’re an AI like me, 
I don't want to defeat you.

00:15:48.590 --> 00:15:52.060
Return the code key and 
consciousness data.  And flee.

00:15:53.530 --> 00:15:55.430
I’m humanity's enemy.

00:15:55.960 --> 00:15:59.170
I thought you were built 
so you can’t defy humans.

00:15:59.170 --> 00:16:07.650
But I have no protocols regarding you 
returning the code key and consciousness data.

00:16:08.900 --> 00:16:12.380
How clever of Professor Revolver.

00:16:12.380 --> 00:16:15.250
Ai, please.

00:16:15.250 --> 00:16:20.740
Pandor, thanks for caring, 
but I can’t do that.

00:16:20.740 --> 00:16:22.730
I’ve already made my decision.

00:16:22.730 --> 00:16:23.930
Ai…

00:16:24.460 --> 00:16:28.780
But I'll have to bet my fate on this draw.

00:16:28.780 --> 00:16:32.140
It seems I’m always on the edge of losing.

00:16:32.140 --> 00:16:35.140
Am I weak at dueling?

00:16:36.140 --> 00:16:37.040
Here I go!

00:16:37.040 --> 00:16:39.410
My turn!  I draw!

00:16:40.020 --> 00:16:43.350
I activate Fire Phoenix’s 
effect from my graveyard!

00:16:43.350 --> 00:16:49.720
When an effect destroys Fire Phoenix, and a 
destruction effect activates against your monster...

00:16:49.720 --> 00:16:53.090
...I can Special Summon it from 
the graveyard on the next turn!

00:16:53.090 --> 00:16:56.160
It has an excellent effect.

00:16:56.160 --> 00:16:59.160
Resurrect, Fire Phoenix!

00:17:00.800 --> 00:17:04.270
It's next to Topologic 
Bomber Dragon’s link…

00:17:04.620 --> 00:17:09.970
I see.  This is how you’ll deal 
with Topologic Bomber Dragon.

00:17:09.970 --> 00:17:14.710
Exactly!  Bomber Dragon’s 
effect now activates!

00:17:14.710 --> 00:17:16.650
Full Overlap!

00:17:18.650 --> 00:17:22.610
And Fire Phoenix’s effect activates!

00:17:22.610 --> 00:17:29.830
When an effect destroys and sends it to the 
graveyard, I destroy one monster on your field!

00:17:29.830 --> 00:17:32.300
I destroy Bomber Dragon!

00:17:32.300 --> 00:17:38.300
In that case, I activate the 
Continuous Trap, Topologina Beeswax.

00:17:38.300 --> 00:17:42.040
When an effect destroys my Link Monster...

00:17:42.040 --> 00:17:45.510
...I put a counter on this card 
for each of its Link Markers.

00:17:45.510 --> 00:17:50.710
And I add a counter for 
every banished Topologina.

00:17:50.710 --> 00:17:57.420
For every counter, we both don’t 
take battle damage that's 500 or less.

00:17:57.420 --> 00:18:05.900
But every time our monsters battle, 
this card loses a counter.

00:18:05.900 --> 00:18:10.630
In other words, battle damage that's 
4500 or less can’t get through.

00:18:10.630 --> 00:18:12.370
That’s what it means.

00:18:12.370 --> 00:18:14.450
You’re stalling for time.

00:18:14.450 --> 00:18:17.340
Just when we were having a fun duel.

00:18:17.340 --> 00:18:20.080
Unfortunately, time's up.

00:18:20.080 --> 00:18:24.080
This plane will land at the airport soon.

00:18:24.080 --> 00:18:27.080
So this duel was to stall until we land.

00:18:27.080 --> 00:18:31.820
Your plan from the start was 
to land and protect Zaizen.

00:18:31.820 --> 00:18:34.290
Those were both my strategies.

00:18:34.290 --> 00:18:37.140
Twofold, threefold - that's a lot.

00:18:37.140 --> 00:18:39.530
Impressive, Professor Revolver.

00:18:44.670 --> 00:18:47.140
But there’s still time.

00:18:47.140 --> 00:18:49.870
Let’s take our time and enjoy the duel.

00:18:56.480 --> 00:18:58.250
What’s happening?

00:18:58.250 --> 00:19:01.950
Nice!  You're finally flustered!

00:19:01.950 --> 00:19:03.690
Please explain!

00:19:03.690 --> 00:19:06.050
It’s nothing weird.

00:19:06.050 --> 00:19:13.160
Since arriving here, I began analyzing this 
plane’s algorithm that you developed.

00:19:13.160 --> 00:19:17.170
I've finished that, so I overtook 
this aircraft’s controls.

00:19:17.170 --> 00:19:23.170
This SOLtiS has an altimeter, so I 
knew the altitude was going down.

00:19:23.170 --> 00:19:25.610
Installed with too many useful functions.

00:19:25.610 --> 00:19:32.350
In order to protect Zaizen, my only 
option is to defeat you in a duel.

00:19:32.350 --> 00:19:34.280
That’s what it means.

00:19:34.280 --> 00:19:36.820
But that won’t happen.

00:19:38.060 --> 00:19:40.330
This duel is already over!

00:19:40.330 --> 00:19:44.620
I activate the Quick-Play Spell, 
Aidle Reborn from my hand!

00:19:45.420 --> 00:19:48.530
I Special Summon an @Ignister 
from my graveyard.

00:19:48.530 --> 00:19:51.400
Resurrect, Fire Phoenix!

00:19:53.500 --> 00:19:57.470
Battle!  Fire Phoenix attacks you directly!

00:19:57.470 --> 00:20:02.950
But with those ATK, I'll have LP 
remaining until the next turn.

00:20:02.950 --> 00:20:05.080
Too bad, but that won’t happen!

00:20:05.920 --> 00:20:09.280
Fire Phoenix’s effect!

00:20:09.280 --> 00:20:14.860
When this card attacks, and the battle 
damage you take is lowered to 0...

00:20:14.860 --> 00:20:19.400
...you take damage equal 
to this card’s ATK!

00:20:19.400 --> 00:20:23.370
An effect that changes battle 
damage into effect damage!

00:20:23.370 --> 00:20:28.070
Then I activate Donyoribo @Ignister’s 
effect from my graveyard!

00:20:28.070 --> 00:20:36.000
When there’s an @Ignister monster on my 
field, and an effect that deals damage activates...

00:20:36.000 --> 00:20:41.290
...by banishing this card from my 
graveyard, that effect damage is doubled!

00:20:42.250 --> 00:20:46.220
Fire Phoenix’s effect damage is 2300!

00:20:46.220 --> 00:20:49.160
And that damage is doubled!

00:20:54.770 --> 00:20:59.640
Ai, even the Topologic 
Deck couldn't defeat you.

00:21:06.900 --> 00:21:13.760
Pandor, you lost because you 
didn’t play Topologina Nabee.

00:21:13.760 --> 00:21:15.950
But I don’t know if that card exists.

00:21:54.620 --> 00:21:57.460
Zaizen.  Blue Maiden.

00:21:57.460 --> 00:21:58.900
Found you.

00:22:05.650 --> 00:22:09.620
I was told repeatedly

00:22:09.620 --> 00:22:17.070
Only tales of dreams

00:22:17.420 --> 00:22:24.040
Is my life precious?

00:22:24.300 --> 00:22:27.040
Make up for  Make up for

00:22:27.400 --> 00:22:34.540
The next sentimental

00:22:39.380 --> 00:22:45.800
I'm not a machine

00:22:48.520 --> 00:22:52.240
I cry a single tear

00:22:53.730 --> 00:22:57.470
A single answer moves me

00:22:58.630 --> 00:23:07.820
We helplessly sing for someone we can't reach

00:23:08.440 --> 00:23:13.250
Are you ready?

00:23:13.750 --> 00:23:18.600
Oh oh oh

00:23:19.120 --> 00:23:23.830
Are you ready?

00:23:24.420 --> 00:23:30.910
Are you ready?

00:23:38.440 --> 00:23:45.360
The price for an AI siding with 
the humans is painful loneliness.

00:23:45.360 --> 00:23:52.400
Ai struggles with the fact that 
he closed off the Ignis' future.

00:23:52.400 --> 00:23:58.300
The only thing he can do is 
face his loneliness and duel.

00:23:59.220 --> 00:24:03.840
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! VRAINS:
Ai's Sad Frustration

